course: dictionary
lesson: 10601
title: Underwear: clothes next to your skin
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Underwear is the clothing you wear next to your skin, under your other clothes. Context gives you the clue: «Clean underwear and socks are worn every day, because they hold sweat and germs.» Underwear is worn every day under your clothes, so it must be the clothes next to your skin.
explain: «Clothes go on in order: underwear first, then clothes, then socks and shoes.» The order tells you that underwear comes before your other clothes. Try your meaning in the sentence: "underwear first, then your clothes" still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Some words for underwear are jokes. «Unmentionables» is a humorous word for underwear: it sounds secret and posh, but everyone knows what it means. Look at the words around a word, and ask what would fit there.
explain: Words can change meaning between countries. In America «pants» means trousers; in Britain «pants» means underwear. Context clues help, and a dictionary settles it.
fact: Underwear is clothing you wear next to your skin, under your other clothes.
fact: Underwear includes pants, knickers, briefs, vests and bras.
fact: Clean underwear is worn every day, because it holds sweat and germs.
fact: «Thermal underwear» is warm underwear for cold weather.
fact: The PANTS rule: the parts covered by underwear are private, so nobody should touch them or ask to see them, and you should always tell a trusted adult if they do.
exercise: «Clean underwear and socks are worn every day, because they hold sweat and germs.» Why should underwear be clean? | Because it is a funny word | *Because it holds sweat and germs | Because it makes you taller | Because it is quicker to put on
exercise: «Clothes go on in order: underwear first, then clothes, then socks and shoes.» What goes on first? | *Underwear | Socks | Clothes | Shoes
exercise: In America «pants» means trousers. If an American praises your pants, what do they mean? | *Your trousers | Your underwear | Your shoes | Your socks
test: Which of these is NOT underwear? | *Gloves | Briefs | Bra | Vest
test: «Thermal underwear» is worn for what? | *Warmth in cold weather | Playing football | Swimming in the sea | Keeping cool in summer
exam: Why are the parts covered by underwear private? | Because they are ugly | Because they are cold | Because underwear is expensive | *Because nobody should touch them or ask to see them
